  "source_review": {
    "review": [
      "cyclicColumnIndex has the literal prefix/wrapped index formula h+((j+(k-h))%t); its injection and exact range are proved, including h=0 and s=t. Actual U submatrices give orthonormal rank-(h+s) frames and exactly the prior selected span projector.",
      "countedTieStructure fixes the above/tied/take sizes by exact finite comparisons sigma[a]<sigma[k] and sigma[a]\u2264sigma[k]; the entire threshold block follows the supplied SVD ordering. No finite-subtype enumeration or existential basis selection is used for the frame entries.",
      "explicitFirstFrames is a fixed expression of the supplied ValidSVD and rank allowance. It uses the positive-threshold counted cyclic family or the literal prefix fallback, covers the zero-tail and large-rank cases, and has count\u2264min(m,l)+1 and width\u2264min(m,l).",
      "The deterministic family is fixed before any comparator or child Completion response. Every actual completion family and every minimum of actual errors satisfy feasibility, the strict positive comparator estimate, and exact zero-error recovery."
    ],
    "limits": "These are exact mathematical frame/count formulas. A program that scans singular values, computes the wrapped indices and copies the selected entries into machine memory, plus recursive assembly and total polynomial CostThrough, remains a separate obligation. No extracted computational implementation or full Target is claimed."
  },
